 NEW YORK--(BUSINESS WIRE)--Elio Mortgage, an AI-native mortgage company redesigning how home loans are originated, today emerged from stealth with $5.1 million in pre-seed funding led by Motive Partners and Social Leverage, with Jeff Horing, co-founder and managing director of Insight Partners, participating as an angel investor.
The company was founded by Oren Michaely, whose background spans engineering at Microsoft and Director of AI at Motive Partners, and Arad Lev Ari, who previously worked in real estate investing and investment banking at KKR and Deutsche Bank. Elio is redesigning mortgage origination end-to-end, using AI to transform how mortgage companies operate and ultimately aim to rewrite the economics of originating a loan. The funding will support continued product development, the expansion of Elio's licensed mortgage operations nationwide, and the recruitment of loan officers as the company scales its AI-native brokerage model.
