 SAN FRANCISCO--(BUSINESS WIRE)--Mona today announced an oversubscribed $3.5M round to expand its AI platform for small business capital access and financial coaching. The round was led by Sandberg Bernthal Venture Partners, with participation from Alumni Ventures, Wisdom Ventures, angels including former Google CEO Eric Schmidt, and others. Mona is also backed by the Mastercard Strive USA Innovation Fund.
Small business owners navigate a fragmented ecosystem of lenders, government programs, grants, and other capital sources – without the financial teams or advisors available to larger companies. Mona brings that fragmented market into one place through its AI platform. Entrepreneurs complete a common application, which Mona uses to surface relevant opportunities, streamline applications, and tailor guidance.
Mona – recently named to Fast Company’s World Changing Ideas List – pairs AI with human coaching, offering ongoing support beyond a one-time funding search.
